From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 10:56:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 36/43] minimize: tell Firefox windows with the same tab title
 apart

Two Firefox windows whose selected tabs had the same title showed the
same tab count. While the session file lagged behind a tab switch, the
switching window matched the other window's count and kept it, because
an ambiguous title matched nothing and the remembered count stayed.

Each window now keeps its last 8 selected-tab titles. Windows and
session windows with the same selected title are paired by how many of
those titles the session window's tabs have; a window takes its single
best session window unless another window claims it with an equal or
higher score. Windows the file cannot tell apart get no count and lose
the remembered one; windows the file does not list yet keep theirs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

